# Leave this UNSET for local development.
#
# When unset, the app calls the API on the SAME HOSTNAME the page was loaded
# from (http://<hostname>:8000). That is required for privacy, not just
# convenience: the one-time anonymous-analysis limit relies on a SameSite=Lax
# cookie, and browsers treat "localhost" and "127.0.0.1" as different sites.
# Opening http://localhost:5173 while the API is addressed as 127.0.0.1:8000
# makes every request cross-site, the cookie is never stored, and the anonymous
# limit is silently bypassed (verified in a real browser).
#
# Only set this if the API genuinely runs on a different host, and use the
# same hostname style you open the app with:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
